[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: A process restart keeps the old interpreter environment

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[WORK]
UID: WORK-DEVENV-PROCESS-ENV-STALE
TITLE: A process restart keeps the old interpreter environment
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
`devenv processes restart` keeps the process's old interpreter environment, so
a devenv.nix change to an interpreter or an env var does not reach a running
scribe or board. The working sequence is `devenv processes down` followed by
`devenv up -d scribe board`, and nothing says so at the point of failure.
Cheapest fix: document the sequence where the processes are defined, or make
the restart path detect a changed environment and re-exec.
<<<
